<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josiah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned c. 640–609 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Josiah was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> from about 640 to 609 BCE. According to the Bible, the discovery of a 'book of the law' in the Temple during his reign led him to carry out a sweeping religious reform, abolishing other cults and centralising worship in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. He was killed at Megiddo in 609 BCE in an encounter with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/necho-ii">Pharaoh Necho II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/josiah.jpg" alt="Josiah" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This image was produced by me, David Castor (user:dcastor). The pictures I submit to the Wikipedia Project are releas... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%85hus_kyrka-12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
